Radiadash
=========

This project implements the RadiaCode serial/BLE protocol based on the
publicly documented, MIT-licensed reverse engineering work in:

  cdump/radiacode — https://github.com/cdump/radiacode
  Copyright (c) Maxim Andreev and contributors
  Licensed under the MIT License.

No source code from that project is copied verbatim into this repository;
the protocol constants and decoding rules were re-implemented in Rust and
cross-checked against the reference implementation.

The .rctrk import format and spectrum interchange conventions follow the
documented RadiaCode application formats and the MIT-licensed parser in
Safecast/safecast-new-map.

Isotope data (from M3 onwards) is derived from publicly available nuclear
data evaluated by NNDC/ENSDF and IAEA; sources are cited per entry.

